# WN22-DC-000050: Windows Server 2022 Kerberos policy user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be limited to seven days or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000050-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Kerberos policy user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be limited to seven days or less.`
    description `This setting determines the period of time (in days) during which a user's Ticket Granting Ticket (TGT) may be renewed. This security configuration limits the amount of time an attacker has to crack the TGT and gain access. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,kerberos-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-2(8)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration >> Policies >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Kerberos Policy >> Maximum lifetime for user ticket renewal to a maximum of "7" days or less.`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by enforcing MaxRenewAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be <= 7 days.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing MaxRenewAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be <= 7 days.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_2_8 `Windows Server implements IA-2(8) by enforcing MaxRenewAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket renewal maximum lifetime must be <= 7 days.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MaxRenewAge`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int <= 7
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
